Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: chip: Use 0x1b0000 TCM RAM base for BCM4345
 rev < 6

brcmf_chip_tcm_rambase() unconditionally returns 0x198000 for
BRCM_CC_4345_CHIP_ID. That is correct for BCM4345C0/43455/43456
(chiprev >= 6), which have 416 KiB of ATCM below the 0x200000 BTCM
base (0x200000 - 0x68000 = 0x198000), but wrong for BCM4345 rev 5
(BCM4345B1, used over PCIe on Apple A8 handhelds such as the iPod
touch 6).

BCM4345B1 has 320 KiB of ATCM (0x50000) and 256 KiB of BTCM
(0x40000) for 576 KiB (0x90000) total RAM starting at 0x1b0000
(0x1b0000..0x240000), confirmed by both iOS 12.4
AppleBCMWLANChipManagerPCIe4345 and the linked entry/vector addresses
of Apple's 43451b1-roml bacchus.trx firmware. Loading firmware at
0x198000 shifts it 96 KiB below ATCM so the ARM CR4 never reaches its
startup code and brcmf_pcie_download_fw_nvram() times out with
"FW failed to initialize".

Return 0x1b0000 for BRCM_CC_4345_CHIP_ID when chiprev < 6, keeping
0x198000 for rev >= 6 (BCM43455/43456) and BRCM_CC_43454_CHIP_ID.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/chip.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/chip.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/chip.c
index 1c6626a5a..94d8c0f24 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/chip.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/chip.c
@@ -711,6 +711,7 @@ static u32 brcmf_chip_tcm_rambase(struct brcmf_chip_priv *ci)
 {
 	switch (ci->pub.chip) {
 	case BRCM_CC_4345_CHIP_ID:
+		return (ci->pub.chiprev < 6) ? 0x1b0000 : 0x198000;
 	case BRCM_CC_43454_CHIP_ID:
 		return 0x198000;
 	case BRCM_CC_4335_CHIP_ID:
